# 2026-08-08: was 1048576 (the checkpoint's full 1M). Nothing here needs it —
# translation chunks are ~4k prompt — and leaving it at 1M meant a single client
# could legally send a 400k-token request. One Hermes --yolo agent did exactly
# that: it held ~40% of the KV pool and every decode step had to stream that KV
# out of LPDDR5X, dragging the shared endpoint from 40 tok/s to 0.3. The API
# stayed up and answered, so it read as a hang.
# 262144 keeps generous headroom for agents while making an oversized request
# fail LOUDLY with HTTP 400 instead of silently starving everyone else.
# 2026-08-08 (lần 2): 262144 -> 294912 = 262144 (context Hermes) + 32768 (max_tokens).
# Lý do: hai giá trị đó cộng lại là prompt+output của một request. Khi max_model_len
# đúng bằng context_length, một agent lấp đầy context rồi xin thêm 32768 output sẽ
# vượt trần và ăn HTTP 400. Nâng trần thay vì hạ context_length, vì hạ context mới là
# thứ chủ máy muốn giữ ở 256K.
# Vẫn AN TOÀN: 294,912 < KV pool 884,281 token, nên đây là trần server GIỮ ĐƯỢC
# (concurrency 3.00x, 1 request tối đa 33% pool). Khác hẳn 1M cũ = 118% pool, tức
# một request đơn lẻ đã vượt cả pool — khai khống, và là cửa gây sự cố starvation.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=294912
# 16 is the validated ceiling for this lane, and the default since 2026-08-06.
# Measured: c6 ~110 tok/s aggregate, c16 218 tok/s (clean 56-chapter batch),
# c32 ~305 tok/s but DEADLOCKS 3/3 at ~12 min — under BOTH cudagraph modes.
#
# Do not raise above 16. Everything from 24 up is measured dead (2026-08-06):
#   c24  wedges almost IMMEDIATELY (~4.4k gen tokens)   RAS EQUAL
#   c30  312 tok/s (+43%) then wedges at ~12 min        RAS EQUAL
#   c32  ~305 tok/s then wedges at ~12 min, 3/3         RAS off-by-one
# So the real ceiling is in (16, 24) — there is no usable middle rung, and c24
# dying fastest means even 20 is suspect. CUDAGRAPH_MODE=PIECEWISE is also
# disproven: zero FULL graphs captured and c32 still wedged, so graph mode is not
# the cause and capping --max-cudagraph-capture-size targets a non-cause.
#
# ONE failure mode, not two: py-spy at both the c24 and c30 wedges shows rank0's
# WorkerAsyncOutputCopy thread stuck in torch.cuda.streams.synchronize while the
# engine waits on shm_broadcast — a GPU-side kernel stall. c32's 1-op RAS skew
# (954063 vs 954062) is NOT proof of dispatch divergence: host enqueue is async,
# so a rank blocked on a stuck kernel can legitimately be one launch ahead. Only
# a large mismatch or missing_ranks>0 would prove divergence.
# Common to every wedge: the fatal step has EVERY request in MTP bonus-token
# state [-1,-1,-1] with total_num_scheduled_tokens = MAX_NUM_SEQS*(MTP+1).
# Necessary, not sufficient — c16 hits that same step at 64 tokens for hours.
# NEXT EXPERIMENT: route sparse-MLA off FlashInfer via the CLI flag
# --attention-backend FLASHMLA_SPARSE (NOT the env var, see below), at c24.
# That aims straight at the kernel stall. Then MTP_NUM_TOKENS=1 at c24/c30.
# CAUTION: 16 dspark/GB10 flags in this file (VLLM_TRITON_MLA_SPARSE,
# VLLM_DSPARK_*, DSPARK_SLOT_CLAMP, ...) are ORPHANS — absent from the compose,
# so they never reach the container. c16's validated-good status was earned with
# all of them inert. Verify with `docker exec ... env` before trusting any of
# them, and don't switch them on in the same run as a concurrency change.
# Full evidence: TransLLM docs/research/c32-deadlock-synthesis.md §7-§8c
MAX_NUM_SEQS=16
MAX_NUM_BATCHED_TOKENS=8192
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.80
# Checkpoint dspark_block_size is 5; upstream requires k >= 5.
MTP_NUM_TOKENS=3
# Default reasoning mode: off, low, high, or max. "low" is DeepSeek V4's
# base thinking mode (no extra effort prefix); request-level overrides still win.
DEFAULT_THINKING=low
# Keep regular CUDA graphs; Anemll auto-enables the slower breakable path
# when this is unset.
